            <ArticleTitle>Estimating the cost of skin cancer detection by dermatology providers in a large healthcare system.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0190-9622(17)32732-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jaad.2017.11.033</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Data on the cost and efficiency of skin cancer detection through total body skin examination (TBSE) are scarce.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To determine the number needed to screen (NNS) and biopsy (NNB) and cost per skin cancer diagnosed in a large dermatology practice in patients undergoing TBSE.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Retrospective observational study.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">From 2011 - 2015, 20,270 patients underwent 33,647 visits for TBSE; 9956 lesion biopsies were performed yielding 2,763 skin cancers, including 155 melanomas. The NNS to detect one skin cancer was 12.2 (95% CI 11.7-12.6) and one melanoma was 215 (95% CI 185-252). The NNB to detect one skin cancer was 3.0 (95% CI 2.9-3.1) and one melanoma was 27.8 (95% CI 23.3-33.3). In a multivariable model for NNS, age and personal history of melanoma were significant factors. Age switches from a protective to a risk factor at 51 years. The estimated cost per melanoma detected was $32,594 (95% CI $27,326-$37,475).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="LIMITATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Data are from a single healthcare system and based on physician coding.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Melanoma detection through TBSE is most efficient in patients over age 50 and those with a personal history of melanoma. Our findings will be helpful in modeling the cost effectiveness of melanoma screening by dermatologists.</AbstractText>
